id":"536a946a-842c-4236-ba01-27046f1f9912","position":{"commit_sha":"9c3fa4ebac43d2f7150de5cdbfa43abe43197284","position":"1788230097201404001-536a946a-842c-4236-ba01-27046f1f9912"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 legitimacy checkpoint (rebar-debug): confirmed the reported mechanism locally by setting `rebar._store.git_locking.fcntl = None`; entering `_store_git_op_lock` and `fetch_coordination_lock` both raises `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'flock'`, matching CI run 33426859481 (`git_locking.py:224` via `_with_index_lock_retry`). However, the repository currently contains an authoritative contrary scope statement in `scripts/check_fcntl_import_guard.py:19-20`: “actually *using* `fcntl` off POSIX is out of scope — Windows is not a declared support target — only that import/collection succeeds.” The commit that added the import guard (5697f2e11179 / ticket 0b31-aeb5-e734-41c9) says the same: “Collectability only; making fcntl locking work on Windows stays out of scope (not a declared support target).” Per the reporter’s explicit guard, this makes the no-fcntl runtime-lock repair a design/support-scope decision rather than an auto-fixable defect. I am not changing production locking code or using force; escalation required to decide whether Windows runtime lock usage is now supported.","timestamp":1788218332610351206},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction: an earlier Phase 1 legitimacy comment on this ticket described the separate `fcntl.flock` Windows failure and belongs to `oxymoronic-industrial-wrasse`. The RCA for THIS ticket is the Windows env-var limit in pytest’s `PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST`: run 33426859481 fails at `_pytest.runner._update_current_test_var` while setting a nodeid containing the 60,000-character `far_over_limit` parameter from `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_outbound_comment_marker_survives_truncation.py`. Local measurement before repair: collected nodeids are 60,163 chars for `far_over_limit` and 75,169 chars for `over_limit_multiline`; simulating the Windows cap raises the same `ValueError` at 60,171 chars. Legitimacy: test-harness defect; product input remains large, only pytest's generated id is unsafe. Attribution: commit 6724e79e8ff857b54dd36a62006a89445fc10ad6 / ticket 5931-78a3-95d2-44cd added the long parametrization without explicit short ids.","timestamp":1788219053206656536},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 RCA refresh: on current origin/main (a22257e7), pytest 9.1.1 writes PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST=f\"{item.nodeid} ({when})\"; collecting this module found two over Windows 32767-char value cap (far_over_limit: 60163/60171, over_limit_multiline: 75169/75177). The RED oracle fails with the exact ValueError. Legitimacy: test-harness defect in the scheduled Windows sweep. Origin: git log -L/blame of the long parametrization points to 6724e79e8ff857b54dd36a62006a89445fc10ad6, verified as rebar-ticket 5931-78a3-95d2-44cd; close class plan_defect. Caller sweep: test-only parametrization, no production callers.","timestamp":1788227110282684001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 2 evidence: RED before fix was `pytest -q -x tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_outbound_comment_marker_survives_truncation.py`, failing at `test_pytest_current_test_values_fit_windows_environment` with `ValueError: the environment variable is longer than 32767 characters`. After adding explicit ids, collect showed `collected=16 over_limit=0` and the long cases had short nodeids `[far_over_limit]` and `[over_limit_multiline]`; focused module passed `15 passed`. Sandboxed mutation evidence (macOS `sandbox-exec` profile allowing writes only under this worktree/.debug-b4f5-sandbox and stdio): replacing both explicit ids with bare tuples returned the held-out test to RED, `MUTATION_EXIT=1`, with the same `ValueError`; the script restored the file. Validation: `make lint` passed, focused+mutate suite `685 passed, 1 skipped`; full local default suite has unrelated baseline failure in `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py::test_relevant_remote_rejection_never_places_candidate_on_shared_head`, reproduced unchanged after restoring this patch. Gerrit change 2469 passed LLM-Review+1 and Verified+1 and was submitted/merged.","timestamp":1788229499449751001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final rebar-debug report: Problem was scheduled Windows sweep run 33426859481 failing before the test body because pytest put huge parametrized text into PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST. Proven root cause: `test_undecorated_text_is_byte_identical_to_the_bare_fitter` used bare tuples for 60k/75k text parameters, so collected nodeids exceeded Windows env-var value limit. Proof: collect-only measured 60171 and 75177 char env-shaped values before fix; RED test failed with the exact ValueError; after explicit ids collect showed over_limit=0 and focused module passed. Origin: commit 6724e79e8ff857b54dd36a62006a89445fc10ad6 / ticket 5931-78a3-95d2-44cd, recorded on close as caused_by with class plan_defect. Test: `test_pytest_current_test_values_fit_windows_environment`; mutation removing explicit ids in macOS sandbox returned it to RED. Fix: only added explicit short pytest ids; large product payloads/assertions unchanged. Scope/safety: test-only, no production callers, no deps, no test weakening. Siblings: candidate long-param nodeid sweep across large-payload tests found over_limit=0 beyond this site; parity axis N/A. Residual risk: unrelated local default-suite baseline failure in `test_atomic_completion_close.py::test_relevant_remote_rejection_never_places_candidate_on_shared_head`, accepted as out of scope because Gerrit Verified passed. Replication: Gerrit change 2469 merged; CI Verified+1 and LLM-Review+1.","timestamp":1788230097201404001}],"created_at":1788217723231066060,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"06ca0ca2-952d-4e90-bf07-81d3d457eb52","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"10b3-1417-67dd-4465"},{"link_uuid":"fb3c30b1-b932-4559-a2c5-16efb2ee26b2","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"5931-78a3-95d2-44cd"}],"description":"## Problem\nThe scheduled Test Suite (mirror) Windows sweep reports `ValueError: the environment variable is longer than 32767 characters` in run 33426859481. Pytest sets `PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST` to `<nodeid> (setup|call|teardown)` for each test. One parametrized test embeds a 60,000-character/75,000-character payload in its generated parameter id, so the Windows environment-variable ceiling is exceeded before the test body runs.\n\n## Root Cause Summary\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_outbound_comment_marker_survives_truncation.py::test_undecorated_text_is_byte_identical_to_the_bare_fitter` parametrizes `(\"label\", \"text\")` with long string values but no explicit short ids. Pytest's default id includes both the short label and the full `text` parameter, producing nodeids measured locally at 60,163 and 75,169 characters. Windows raises `ValueError: the environment variable is longer than 32767 characters` when pytest writes that nodeid into `PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST`.\n\n## Plan\n1. Keep the product payload large; only shorten pytest's generated parameter IDs by giving the long cases explicit ids derived from the existing `label` values.\n2. Add a regression test in the same module that collects this module's nodeids from `request.session.items`, constructs pytest's real env value shape (`f\"{item.nodeid} (setup)\"`, also representative for teardown), and passes it through a small test-local `_assert_windows_env_value_fits` seam that implements Windows' documented 32767-character single-env-var ceiling and raises the exact `ValueError` message. This is RED on current code because the collected nodeid itself is too long; it is GREEN only when pytest would stop writing overlong `PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST` values.\n3. Verify the sibling set by collecting the module and listing all nodeids over the Windows cap; the repair must reduce the set to zero while preserving the existing large-payload product assertions.\n4. Attribute the defect by blaming the long parametrization and citing commit `6724e79e8ff857b54dd36a62006a89445fc10ad6` / `rebar-ticket: 5931-78a3-95d2-44cd`.\n5. Run the focused module, a sandboxed mutation check that removes the explicit ids and confirms the new test returns to RED, then `make lint` and the default suite before Gerrit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] CI run 33426859481's failing test/helper is identified as pytest writing `PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST` for the long parametrized nodeids in `test_outbound_comment_marker_survives_truncation.py`.\n- [x] The RED test constructs `PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST`-shaped values from real collected nodeids and fails through `_assert_windows_env_value_fits` with the same `ValueError` text when any exceeds 32767 characters.\n- [x] After the fix, no nodeid in that module produces a `PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST` value over 32767 characters.\n- [x] The original large-input assertions still execute with the 60,000-character and multiline payloads; only pytest ids change.\n- [x] The RCA records the legitimacy verdict, sibling sweep result, and caused-by attribution to ticket `5931-78a3-95d2-44cd`.\n- [x] [non-codebase] Mutation check removing the explicit ids makes the RED test fail again inside the sandbox.\n  provenance: environment=debug-b4f5-pytestid macOS sandbox-exec; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=simulation — defect-seeded local mutation removed explicit pytest ids inside a sandbox permitting writes only under the worktree and .debug-b4f5-sandbox, and the held-out test failed with the exact Windows env-var ValueError before the script restored the file.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_outbound_comment_marker_survives_truncation.py","reason":"Add short pytest parameter ids and a Windows PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST length regression assertion."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","10b3-1417-67dd-4465"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"8d0eec3b-0035-4b83-977d-30016846f9cd","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["navapbc/rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","status_fork_resolutions":[{"dropped_uuid":"9d88edd1-fb96-4e3c-8f53-955831d77723","winner_uuid":"8d0eec3b-0035-4b83-977d-30016846f9cd"}],"tags":["ci","windows","debugging"],"ticket_id":"b4f5-11c0-8633-4204","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep hits 32767-character environment variable limit in tests","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["bc283eb5-4f17-4654-99d3-7aaeea4927be","8d0eec3b-0035-4b83-977d-30016846f9cd","1d77cff3-0c96-4465-87e1-d0fce313d851","d6a2e275-bde8-4449-926e-f51c868aeeb8","06ca0ca2-952d-4e90-bf07-81d3d457eb52","02b55c32-8ff1-4650-aa3d-87cfe5caa3ab","a86e7b50-5572-432a-8100-e6583ba1af71","098b944a-4ad3-41e7-af36-24cfbf4fef64","b43b15f4-7c0d-4aed-93af-0bdbe8718c03","9d88edd1-fb96-4e3c-8f53-955831d77723","81c5b04b-b7ae-403e-a915-5ce90615be4b","fb3c30b1-b932-4559-a2c5-16efb2ee26b2","536a946a-842c-4236-ba01-27046f1f9912"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788236556257343368,"uuid":"5514937b-bcea-42fa-bd1e-69e3eca3ab03"}